{
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Step 1: the worked example\nThe teacher deploys the OMG *Incident management* model twice: first the original, then an adapted version. Watch, then answer.",
      "id": "class_s01_part_a_0"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**Feedback.** {{fbPartA}}",
      "conditional": {
        "hide": "=fbPartA = null or fbPartA = \"\""
      },
      "id": "class_s01_part_a_1"
    },
    {
      "type": "checklist",
      "key": "a1",
      "label": "1. Which errors did the original model produce on deploy? (select all that apply)",
      "values": [
        {
          "label": "The process is not marked executable",
          "value": "notExecutable"
        },
        {
          "label": "The gateways have no conditions",
          "value": "noConditions"
        },
        {
          "label": "The message start event names no message",
          "value": "noMessage"
        },
        {
          "label": "The tasks have no assignee",
          "value": "noAssignee"
        },
        {
          "label": "The diagram has lanes",
          "value": "lanes"
        }
      ],
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      },
      "id": "class_s01_part_a_2"
    },
    {
      "type": "radio",
      "key": "a2",
      "label": "2. In the adapted model, what does the gateway \"Can handle myself?\" read?",
      "values": [
        {
          "label": "The variable canHandle",
          "value": "canHandle"
        },
        {
          "label": "The lane of the account manager",
          "value": "lane"
        },
        {
          "label": "What the person decides, without any variable",
          "value": "person"
        }
      ],
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      },
      "id": "class_s01_part_a_3"
    },
    {
      "type": "radio",
      "key": "a3",
      "label": "3. The first instance was completed with no variables. Which way did it go?",
      "values": [
        {
          "label": "To Handle 1st level issue: canHandle did not exist, so the default flow was taken",
          "value": "default"
        },
        {
          "label": "To Explain solution: with no variable the answer is yes",
          "value": "yes"
        },
        {
          "label": "Nowhere: the instance stopped with an incident",
          "value": "incident"
        }
      ],
      "validate": {
        "required": true
      },
      "id": "class_s01_part_a_4"
    }
  ],
  "type": "default",
  "id": "class-s01-part-a",
  "executionPlatform": "Camunda Cloud",
  "executionPlatformVersion": "8.9.0",
